; voice-track-run.fk — renders every tongue of a prepared track to the end, one GPU client at a time.
; For each tongue it runs the supervisor (voice-track.bml): it writes the request, then LOOKS at the worker's record in the shared field
; (the worker is the host's service, docs/launchd/earth.hati.voice-track-worker.plist; this run begins nothing). A worker that says it is
; working and has given no beat for 150 s is ended with host_signal; the host's manager brings the next. Prints, per tongue, how many
; times the GPU wait wedged (-1 = no service was there to render: the operator has not loaded the service).
; Needs observe/voice-track-prepare-run.fk to have run, and observe/voice-g2p-grow-run.fk for any word the tables lack.
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/voice-track.bml
(do
    (defn vt-say (code w) (print_str (str_concat code (str_concat " wedges " (int_to_str w)))))
    (vt-say "en" (vtr-supervise "en" 0 0))
    (vt-say "pt" (vtr-supervise "pt" 0 0))
    (vt-say "fa" (vtr-supervise "fa" 0 0))
    (vt-say "id" (vtr-supervise "id" 0 0))
    0)
